From f9af8b6c0fc95eb801b4fcb7d01961d03b275cee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:47:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Remembered cards of an owner the Board no longer
 carries are released as it last reported them

Problem: 2026-11-18. After workers 2-8 were removed from the Board, 68 hub chats listed 1,231 finished cards and
28 MacBook chats 1,409 as unfinished `unknown` rows (reported_status done or archived), for good.

Why 1: each is a remembered origin-work row (`_legacy_remote_links` carries the previous projection's rows whose
record the replica no longer has), still `unknown`/unreleased.
Why 2: the Board drops a removed machine's records, so no record is left to attest the completion, and no rule
releases a remembered row without one ("absence is never closure").
Why 3: that rule was written for ONE missing record of an owner that is otherwise present (evicted copies,
reprovisioned owners); the removal of the whole owner had no case of its own.
Root (happened): removing a machine leaves every unconfirmed card it finished as a permanent obligation of the
chats that handed it work. (Cards the owner attested before going silent are released since 6721503d602; this is
the remainder: rows already remembered unreleased when the owner disappeared.)
Root (not caught): no test removed an owner from the replica; an operator edit of the durable snapshot does not
hold either, because every running process keeps the rows in memory and writes them back within seconds.

Fix: `_release_removed_owners` (kanban_session_activity_records): in a replica that is not stale and carries task
records, a remembered, qualified row whose owner gateway publishes no task record at all and has no fresh scope
heartbeat, and whose last reported status is done or archived, reads released with that status (`owner_removed:
True`). Unchanged: open and unknown-status rows, unqualified rows, any row of an owner that still publishes another
card or beats, and everything while the replica is stale or carries no task record. The release is remembered
like any other row (later reads and the durable snapshot keep it).

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_release_removed_owner_rows.py (the pure rule and its controls; OwnerSink;
`_legacy_remote_links` over a real replica file and durable snapshot: a removed owner's done card is released and
stays released, its open card and a still-publishing owner's dropped record are not; a stale replica releases
nothing). Dry run of the patched projection on the MacBook's live data: stuck finished rows 1,409 -> 53 (23 of an
owner that is alive, the rest unqualified rows). Untested: a replica mid-resync that is fresh yet lacks an owner's
records; the Desktop render.

